course: dictionary
lesson: 5220
title: Jeans: a word for clothes
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Jeans are trousers made of strong cotton cloth called denim, usually blue. Context clues help you work out the meaning. «A pair of jeans» tells you the word is plural, so we say «jeans are», not «jeans is».
explain: Look at the words around the word. «Some schools have non-uniform days when pupils can wear jeans.» Non-uniform means not the usual school clothes, so jeans are everyday clothes for play and weekends.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping in a different word. «Metal rivets on jeans stop pockets tearing.» Put in trousers: «Metal rivets on trousers stop pockets tearing» still makes sense, so jeans are a kind of trousers.
fact: Jeans are trousers made of denim, a strong cotton cloth, usually blue.
fact: Jeans is a plural word: say «a pair of jeans», not «a jean».
fact: Jeans were first made strong for miners and workers in America in the nineteenth century.
fact: Metal rivets on jeans were patented in 1873 to stop pockets tearing on miners' work trousers.
fact: Jeans are woven with blue threads one way and white threads the other, so the inside looks paler than the outside.
exercise: «That is why jeans go pale and why one red sock can turn a whole wash pink.» What does pale mean here? | Very long and thin | Dark and shiny | *Lighter in colour, faded | Wet and cold
exercise: «Some schools have non-uniform days when pupils can wear jeans.» What does non-uniform mean? | *Not the usual school clothes | Clothes that are very expensive | A school trip | Clothes made of wool
exercise: Jeans are made of a cloth called denim. What is denim? | *A strong cotton cloth | A kind of bread | A metal used for buttons | A thin, see-through paper
test: «Metal rivets on jeans were patented in 1873 to stop pockets tearing on miners' work trousers.» Why were the rivets added? | *To stop pockets tearing | To show the jeans' name | To make the jeans turn pale | To make the jeans colder
test: Which sentence uses jeans correctly? | A jeans is new. | That jeans is new. | *Those jeans are new. | Jeans is new.
exam: «Jeans are woven with blue threads one way and white threads the other, which is why the inside is paler than the outside.» What makes the inside of jeans look paler? | The jeans were bleached on purpose | *The white threads show more on the inside | The inside is a different cloth from the outside
